+# MIxS anchors its own structured patterns (^...$). From linkml-runtime 1.12 a pattern whose
+# partial_match is not true is also wrapped as ^(?:...)$, so those anchors come out doubled.
+# Set partial_match: true on those patterns, as MIxS already does for most of its anchored
+# patterns. linkml 1.12 then adds no wrapper, and the MIxS anchors still require a full match.
+# Stripping the anchors instead would leave them unanchored in submission-schema, which builds
+# with linkml-runtime 1.9.5 and adds no anchors of its own.
+# The two slots are named because partial_match: true is only safe when the anchors cover every
+# alternative, as in ^(a|b)$ but not ^a|b$. tests/test_structured_pattern_anchors.py fails if
+# another MIxS pattern arrives anchored without partial_match, so a new one gets reviewed here.
+# See https://github.com/microbiomedata/nmdc-schema/issues/3579.
+(.slots | (.cult_root_med, .genetic_mod) | select(.structured_pattern and (.structured_pattern.syntax | test("^\\^\\(.*\\)\\$$"))) | .structured_pattern.partial_match) = true |
+
